  <h1>Air Conditioning Advice for York</h1>
  <p>If you already know us for boilers, it's the same faces and the same standards turning up for air conditioning — the city we've called home for 18 years. Here's what York homeowners and small businesses ask us most.</p>

  <h2>Home air conditioning in York</h2>
  <p>One room needing cooling — a bedroom, a home office, a loft conversion — a single-split system is usually all you need: one unit outside, one in. We size it on a free visit rather than guessing over the phone, because an oversized unit just costs you more to run for no real benefit.</p>
  <p>See our <a href="/air-conditioning-domestic-york/">Domestic Air Conditioning in York</a> page for more.</p>

  <h2>Single vs multi-split — which do you need?</h2>
  <p>Cooling more than one room? A multi-split system lets several indoor units share a single outdoor unit, so you're not left with a wall of boxes outside. It tends to suit bigger York homes, or a small business with two or three rooms that all need cooling.</p>
  <p>See our <a href="/air-conditioning-split-systems-york/">Single &amp; Multi-Split Air Conditioning</a> page for the full breakdown.</p>

  <h2>Air conditioning for York small businesses</h2>
  <p>Shops, offices and small units get exactly the same standard of install we'd put into a home — proper sizing, proper commissioning — and we'll fit around your trading hours wherever we can. A service contract means you're not finding out a unit's packed in on the first hot day of the year.</p>
  <p>See our <a href="/air-conditioning-commercial-york/">Air Conditioning for Small Businesses in York</a> page.</p>

  <h2>Brands and standards</h2>
  <p>We fit Bosch, Daikin and Haier, and we're F-Gas registered — that's the certification for handling refrigerant safely, separate from Gas Safe, which covers boilers. We don't publish the F-Gas number online for security reasons, but happy to give it to you directly if you ask.</p>

  <h2>Book a York visit</h2>
  <p>Single room, whole house, or a shop full of customers who'd rather not swelter — we're in York every week. Call and tell us what needs cooling; you'll get a straight answer, not a sales pitch.</p>
